  "ai_overview": {
    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "High blood pressure (hypertension) is treated using a combination of heart-healthy lifestyle changes and, if needed, prescription medications.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "heart-healthy lifestyle changes and, if needed, prescription medications"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Lifestyle Changes"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "DASH Diet: Eat a diet rich in fruits, vegetables, whole grains, and low-fat dairy while lowering sodium (salt) to under 1,500\u20132,300 mg per day."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Physical Activity: Get regular aerobic exercise, like brisk walking, cycling, or swimming for at least 30 minutes most days."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Weight Management: Aim for a healthy weight, as losing even a small percentage of body weight helps lower pressure."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Limit Alcohol and Quit Smoking: Reduce alcohol to no more than one drink a day for women and two for men, and stop smoking."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Stress Management: Find healthy ways to reduce chronic stress through relaxation, meditation, or adequate sleep."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "First-Line Medications"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "When lifestyle habits are not enough, doctors prescribe first-line blood pressure medications:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "ACE Inhibitors: Relax and widen blood vessels by blocking a hormone that constricts them (e.g., lisinopril)."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Angiotensin Receptor Blockers (ARBs): Block blood-vessel constricting hormones similarly to ACE inhibitors without causing a dry cough (e.g., losartan)."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Calcium Channel Blockers: Help the heart relax and widen blood vessels by blocking calcium entering cells (e.g., amlodipine)."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Thiazide Diuretics (\"Water Pills\"): Help the body get rid of excess sodium and water (e.g., chlorthalidone, hydrochlorothiazide)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "You can learn more about managing these choices through the National Institutes of Health or the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention .",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "National Institutes of Health",
            "link": "https://www.nhlbi.nih.gov/health/high-blood-pressure/treatment"
          },
          {
            "text": "Centers for Disease Control and Prevention",
            "link": "https://www.cdc.gov/high-blood-pressure/living-with/index.html"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, share:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Your recent blood pressure readings"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Any other health conditions you have (like diabetes or kidney disease)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can give you more tailored information to discuss with your doctor."
      }
    ],
